A :BEGINCASE holding only an :OTHERWISE clause, which the compiler
rejects: begincase_requires_case fires on the :BEGINCASE token when the
:ENDCASE closes it (diag.begincase_requires_case). missing_otherwise must
not fire, since an :OTHERWISE is present.
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE PickShelf;
	:PARAMETERS sZone;
	:DECLARE sShelf;
	:BEGINCASE;
	:OTHERWISE;
		sShelf := "A-" + sZone;
		:EXITCASE;
	:ENDCASE;
	:RETURN sShelf;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE PickShelf;
	:PARAMETERS sZone;
	:DECLARE sShelf;

	:BEGINCASE;
	:OTHERWISE;
		sShelf := "A-" + sZone;
		:EXITCASE;
	:ENDCASE;

	:RETURN sShelf;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
4:2-4:12 error begincase_requires_case: ':BEGINCASE' requires at least one ':CASE' block
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
4:2-4:12 error begincase_requires_case: ':BEGINCASE' requires at least one ':CASE' block
